       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risks include lactic acidosis and severe GI intolerance, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
